          "block_content": "More than three-quarters of young Chinese consumers are thus most interested in buying iconic styles that are easily recognizable, with the trend most prevalent among the post-'65s/'70s consumers. Indeed, the concept of a niche brand has multiple meanings across luxury segments, from one that exhibits unique design to those that are niche in the sense of being rarely seen on the street, or simply not available in mainland China.",
